## Accessible view

### Physical picture

{% if physics_ir and physics_ir.dynamics.expected_equation_type == "topology_only" %}
The task asks for a topological characterization rather than a dynamical
equation. The Agent evaluates the winding or topological charge of the declared
`{{ physics_ir.order_parameter.topology_field }}` field using the stated profile
and boundary conditions.
{% elif physics_ir and physics_ir.dynamics.type == "sigma_model" %}
The central field is the antiferromagnetic order parameter
`{{ physics_ir.order_parameter.primary }}`. Its collective motion is inertial,
so acceleration and damping can appear after projection onto the selected
coordinates. In the compensated limit, the ferromagnetic gyrotropic term must
cancel.
{% elif physics_ir and physics_ir.dynamics.type == "llg" %}
The central field is the normalized magnetization
`{{ physics_ir.order_parameter.primary }}`. The field obeys first-order LLG
dynamics; projection onto a rigid texture produces a gyrotropic collective
equation when the topology is nonzero.
{% elif physics_ir %}
The selected order parameter is `{{ physics_ir.order_parameter.primary }}` and
the candidate dynamics class is `{{ physics_ir.dynamics.type }}`. This class
requires expert review before a final equation can be claimed.
{% endif %}

